content.text:
Neither first idea improved the incumbent. Repeated digits lost 2 nats, which makes sense: multiples of 11 up to 100 are exactly the repdigits, so the incumbent already has that rule. The parity veto gained only 0.2 nats. I'm now fitting three more single changes in the background:
- a separate evidence strength for each set size, aimed at the critique's two-example dip;
- extra prior weight on ranges whose edges sit at the smallest or largest example;
- a prior expectation that ranges are narrow.

I'll get a notification when those fits finish.

